cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "caiso-siting: node-level intelligence from CAISO interconnection filings"
message: "If you use this software or its outputs in research or publication, please cite it and cite the upstream data sources separately."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karimov
    given-names: Robert
repository-code: "https://github.com/mrk-svg/caiso-siting"
abstract: >-
  An open-source pipeline that reads the California ISO public interconnection
  queue reports, Transmission Plan Deliverability allocation results, Local
  Capacity Technical Reports, PG&E's wholesale distribution queue and EIA-860,
  and publishes one page per interconnection node: what has been filed there,
  what share of filings survived each process gate, what deliverability was
  requested and refused by allocation group, and what is already built. It
  states no causes, produces no composite scores and estimates no dollar
  figures; every figure carries the source file and run date it came from.
keywords:
  - interconnection queue
  - CAISO
  - energy storage
  - transmission plan deliverability
  - local capacity requirement
  - open data
license: MIT
